course: dictionary
lesson: 1004
title: A word from the cotton field
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one special subject. «Boll» is a word from farming and science. You may not know it, but the words around it can help: plant, seeds, fluffy and cotton.
explain: Read this sentence: «In Alabama the boll weevil ate so much cotton that farmers grew other crops.» A weevil is a beetle, and it eats something from the cotton plant. The boll is the part of the plant that holds the cotton, so the clues point to a seed pod.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. Then swap your meaning into the sentence. A boll is a round seed pod that bursts open, so the beetle eats the pods and the sentence still makes sense. That is a good sign your meaning is right.
fact: A boll is a noun: the round seed pod of the cotton plant, or the flax plant.
fact: When a boll bursts open, it shows fluffy white fibres inside.
fact: The cotton fibres are picked and spun into thread.
fact: The «boll weevil» is a beetle that eats cotton bolls.
fact: In Enterprise, Alabama, people built a statue of the boll weevil, because the beetle made farmers grow other crops.
exercise: «The boll burst open, and white fluffy fibres spilled out.» What is a boll? | *A round seed pod of the cotton plant | A spinning machine | A kind of farm tractor | A fluffy white cloud
exercise: «The boll weevil is a beetle that eats cotton.» What kind of creature is a boll weevil? | A bird that sings | *A beetle | A fish
exercise: «In Alabama the boll weevil ate so much cotton that farmers grew other crops.» What do the words so much cotton suggest? | *The beetle ate a lot of cotton | The cotton was sold at a shop in town | The beetle ate very little cotton | The farmers stopped eating bread
test: Where do the white fibres of cotton come from? | From a bird's nest | *From a boll that bursts open | From a tractor's engine | From the bottom of a river
test: Which word means a round seed pod of the cotton plant? | Bud | Bulb | *Boll | Berry
exam: Why did the farmers in Alabama grow other crops? | Because the boll is a kind of fish | Because farmers prefer to eat beetles | Because cotton plants grow in the sea | *Because the boll weevil ate so much cotton
